menu "Shelly hardware snapshot"

    config SHELLY_HW_SNAPSHOT
        bool "Record a hardware snapshot for the Wi-Fi mode page"
        default n
        help
            For bringing up a board: every 10 s of a normal boot, record the
            relay and input pins, the button, the temperature sensors, the heap
            and the power-meter probe's readings in memory that survives the
            restart into Wi-Fi mode, where the page shows them (/hw.json).
            Costs about 450 bytes of RTC memory and a 3 KB task. Reads only.

endmenu
